  "id": "COMPOUND:38495 - PROTEIN:6010",
  "verbalization": "Pisonin A is implicated in the regulation of Casein kinase I delta through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Pisonin A acts as a target for multiple compounds, with A172 being a common intermediate in these relationships. A172 is a target of Bisdehydrostemonine, 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl-oleanolic acid 28 O-beta-D-glucopyranoside, and 2-Acetoxytridecane, all of which have been linked to the activation of Casein kinase I delta. This indicates that Pisonin A may influence the activity of these compounds, which in turn modulate Casein kinase I delta. The shared involvement of A172 in multiple pathways suggests a potential mechanism where Pisonin A could either directly or indirectly regulate the activity of Casein kinase I delta through the intermediation of these other compounds. The evidence supports a network of interactions where Pisonin A serves as a central node, linking to a series of targets that ultimately affect Casein kinase I delta.",
